<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB to take stake in PBE ELBUD.</title>
<headline>ABB to take stake in PBE ELBUD.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABB AB/AG, the Swiss-Swedish engineering firm, said it had signed an agreement to purchase a controlling interest in PBE ELBUD Krakow.</p>
<p>&quot;ABB is to purchase 60 percent of the company from various Polish National Investment Funds,&quot; ABB said in a statement.</p>
<p>The agreement is subject to regulatory approval.</p>
<p>The company, based in Krakow with 500 employees, is active in the construction and repair of power lines and substations for the Polish national power grid.</p>
<p>ABB said that the company would be called &quot;ABB ELBUD Ltd.&quot;</p>
<p>It will become part of ABB's global power transmission and distribution division, ABB said.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
